draw_text_half: faithful reconstruction of the packed-register texel span loop

The gouraud-textured ground blitter's inner loop is a 1996 register hack (asm
0x4101b7-0x4101f6): the span counter lives in the HIGH 16 bits of ecx packed
with the v coordinate, and the v-step word @0x480038 carries 0xffff/0xfffe in
its high half (prologue 0x410049-0x41005f) so a single add steps v AND
decrements the counter; the texel address is built byte-wise (mov ah,ch /
mov al,bh) into the tpage base @0x46000c and the pixel is CLUT-looked-up by
replacing dl in the clut base @0x460004. Ghidra rendered this as CONCAT31/
SCARRY4 spaghetti that double-dereferenced the texel pointer and never
terminated correctly -> the ground blitter sprayed wild texels (billions of
writes/frame, absorbed by the big native mmap) and the floor/road showed the
sky panorama instead (THE dominant fb-vs-reference defect on every level).
Both the unclipped and clipped row loops are replaced with the exact register
algorithm.

